Z||000003||Shaun41178||08-04-2001||08:07 PM||||Sean you have a 3.4 right?  if so then it might be close.  If you still have the 2.8 then you are toast if you go from stop.  Maybe try racing the guy from 80 and up.  He will probably run out of power with all his drag.  Worth a shot.<P>If not I don't think you have a chance with a 2.8 that is.  Just try it and find out and post the results here||||reg||1
Z||000004||HummelHund||08-04-2001||11:55 PM||||Ford did produce a Lightning model F-150 from 1993-1995. It was equipped with the 351 V8 with some add on performance goodies. It was rated at 240hp and 340 ft.lb of torque, and went 0-60 in 7.6 seconds. <BR>Here's a website with the rest of the specs on the Lightning: <A HREF="http://home.mmcable.com/cool1/specs" TARGET=_blank>http://home.mmcable.com/cool1/specs</A> <BR>Sounds like a fairly mean truck. It should be pretty even against a stock Fiero, but I would make sure he hasn't done any performance upgrades to that engine, 351 performance parts are easy to come by.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe, The "Black Wedge of Death" ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||08-05-2001||01:16 AM||||Yes, I have a 3.4 Fiero, but its not "drivable" at the moment, to say the least...This is against a fairly stock 3.1 stroker, auto tranny.<P>Anyway, It is a completly stock engine, I see it around town too much for him to have done anything to it. Its not an SVT either BTW..I think thats the same website I'm thinking of, also notes the truck is electronically limited to 110, so I could toast it all out. Once my car is done again, I'll race him and see what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000006||JayUSA77||08-05-2001||01:28 AM||||someone posted that the lightning couldnt run 13's there right it runs 12's are at least the 99's do. They come equipped with a super charger right out of the factory. as for the older ones. I dont know its probably BS plus if you jump the line on him which you should you might have enough to take him. I know people that say they run 11's and end up running 14's so BS is all around us. and oh ya good luck and post your results.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||firstfiero||08-05-2001||10:43 AM||||   You can't even compare the lightnings of the early 90's to the svt of 98 to current. They were just big heavy trucks with performance parts. The new lightnings not only have the Triton v8 but it's supercharged. If you see one with altezas thats this years model and it's doing 0 to 60 in 5.2 seconds. Thats f-ing awsome for any car let alone a truck! The are really a complete sports car from their suspension to the fact that they weigh less then an svt cobra. anyway the two trucks aren't even comparable. <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||08-05-2001||03:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JayUSA77:<BR><B>someone posted that the lightning couldnt run 13's there right it runs 12's are at least the 99's do. They come equipped with a super charger right out of the factory. as for the older ones. I dont know its probably BS plus if you jump the line on him which you should you might have enough to take him. I know people that say they run 11's and end up running 14's so BS is all around us. and oh ya good luck and post your results.<BR>J<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ahh 12's??? ,not without some mods.My uncle owns an SVT dealership here in ontario , they campaign 2 / 2001 SVT lightnings , Slicks , chip , shift kit , exhaust work , headers and a few other bolt ons , 12.98's with a very compitent driver is the bestthey have ever turned , this was at a cool night time event.<P>Most of the show room run mid 13's @ best<P><BR>JM <BR>||||reg||1
